    <h1>Computer Science and Engineering (CSE)</h1>

    <h2>Welcome to CSE</h2>

    <p>
        Computer Science and Engineering (CSE) is a field that combines computer science
        with engineering to develop software, applications, computer systems and other
        technologies. It focuses on understanding how computers work and how technology
        can be used to solve real-world problems.
    </p>

    <p>
        CSE is one of the most rapidly developing fields and plays an important role in
        areas such as artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, web development, mobile
        applications, data science, cloud computing, and software engineering.
    </p>

    <h2>What Do CSE Students Learn?</h2>

    <p>
        Students studying CSE learn programming languages, computer networks, databases,
        data structures, algorithms, operating systems, software development,
        and other technologies. Along with technical knowledge, CSE also helps students
        develop problem-solving, logical thinking, creativity and teamwork skills.
    </p>

    <h2>Career Opportunities</h2>

    <p>
        A degree in CSE can lead to many different career opportunities.
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li>Software Developer</li>
        <li>Web Developer</li>
        <li>Mobile App Developer</li>
        <li>Data Analyst</li>
        <li>AI and Machine Learning Engineer</li>
        <li>Cybersecurity Professional</li>
        <li>Cloud Engineer</li>
        <li>Database Administrator</li>
        <li>Game Administrator</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Explore More</h2>

    <p>
        Learn more about the subjects, skills and career opportunities related to CSE on
        our CSE Resources page.
    </p>

